      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.53,
      "end_seconds": 211.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Okay, finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.78,
      "end_seconds": 266.02,
      "duration_seconds": 36.24,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be jaundice with a cause we still need to find, or it might be hepatitis. I'd like to arrange an ultrasound of the abdomen for jaundice. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'll request a hepatitis screen, it'll help with jaundice. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.19,
      "end_seconds": 285.27,
      "duration_seconds": 18.08,
      "text": "please avoid alcohol completely and don't take any painkillers except paracetamol, and not much of that i'm going to send a referral to a liver specialist come back or go to emergency straight away if you vomit blood or become drowsy or confused"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.41,
      "end_seconds": 287.46,
